    "sha": "d9cd719c89b85715063375160c8aec3fb3897286",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGQ5Y2Q3MTljODliODU3MTUwNjMzNzUxNjBjOGFlYzNmYjM4OTcyODY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T22:53:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T22:53:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Sinumerik writes work offsets 5/6 as G505/G506\n\nOn the 840D the settable zero offsets are G54..G57 then G505..G599;\nG58/G59 are axial programmable offsets that select no frame. The post\nwrote the engine's generic G58/G59 verbatim, so a setup on offset 5 or\n6 ran in the wrong frame or alarmed. frameWord maps the word for the\nopening block and for a probe result that sets an offset (frame 6 is\nnow set and re-selected as G506); a word naming no settable frame is\nrefused by name. Decision in docs/decisions/934-sinumerik-g505.md.\n\nFixes #934\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "8eaf30014d67be2772aba44a79e38de6170dc6d1",
